+# Exact-source and prior-attempt gate: 2518 / KOU-21.9
+
+Completed2026-10-02 UTC. Rank413; gate uses no author proof turn.
+
+## Target and edition
+
+Yiftach Barnea, Kourovka Notebook Problem21.9, 21st edition (2026). Given any finite-rank nonabelian free pro-p group F, seek finitely many open subgroups U_i, one equal to F, such that a subgroup K contained in every U_i and characteristic in every U_i must be trivial. All primes p and all finite ranks d>=2 are in scope. It is an existence question for a finite family; excluding only selected characteristic-series terms is insufficient.
+
+The editors' current October2026 full edition was linked by their September30/October1 update. The precise statement appears on printed/PDF177, with no star, sharp sign, solution, or comment. The updates-only PDF contains no entry for21.9. The editors explain that a sharp sign would designate an unverified AI proposal and would still leave a problem unsolved; this problem has no such sign. Primary full PDF: https://kourovkanotebookorg.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/21tkt.pdf ; updates: https://kourovkanotebookorg.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/21upd.pdf ; announcement: https://kourovkanotebookorg.wordpress.com/2026/09/30/october-2026-update-for-the-21st-edition/ . Printed177 was inspected visually. The older January source indexed at https://alglog.org/21tkt.pdf has the same statement on printed163; page numbers must remain edition-specific.
+
+The requested https://www.unsolvedmath.com/problems/2518 was attempted but unavailable through the web tool. The full pinned dataset record was read (revision37e53eabe540fb458758e198be61634bd02ee008), including its2026-08-17 open-status triage. The imported research-results entry is null.
+
+## Exact related primary paper
+
+Barnea, Ershov, Le Boudec, Reid, Vannacci and Weigel, *On commensurators of free groups and free pro-p groups*, arXiv:2507.04120v3, revised22September2026, to appear in Compositio Mathematica. https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.04120v3 . Question4 on printed/PDF53 is the same problem and is expressly left open. This page was visually checked.
+
+Read in particular the introduction, Section3.3–3.5 conventions, Observation6.10 and its proof, Section7.2, and Section12.1–12.2. Observation6.10 proves a two-subgroup analogue for **discrete** free groups of certain ranks. The authors explicitly say they do not know its free-pro-p analogue even for one rank. Their simple tdlc constructions include quotients and do not produce the required family in F. Proposition12.2 has a different requirement involving finitely many individual automorphisms; Question4 asks invariance under the entire automorphism group of each chosen open subgroup. These distinctions prevent substituting a neighboring solved result.
+
+The paper uses continuous automorphisms and topological generation for pro-p groups. It supplies the pro-p Schreier/basis facts in Section3.4, the Frattini basis criterion in Lemma3.9, and the natural epimorphism Aut(F)->GL_d(Z_p) in Notation7.8. Closed derived subgroups are used for pro-p abelianizations. The original question does not explicitly write 'closed' before the quantified subgroup. Our first partial results work for arbitrary subgroups invariant under all continuous automorphisms, so they do not depend on silently inserting that restriction. If a closed-subgroup reformulation is used later, it must be justified by taking closures under continuous automorphisms. Full abstract characteristicity implies invariance under this continuous subgroup of automorphisms, so the necessary conditions also hold with that reading.
+
+## Actual prior-attempt gate
+
+A fresh scan of430 remote refs found no exact-ID/alias branch, target path or commit. All-state PR searches for2518, KOU-21.9, the pro-p21.9 wording and Barnea returned zero. Related-target metadata has no exact entry. Current main queue row413 is queued0/5. These checks do not rule out uncommitted or differently indexed work.
+
+A recovered imported desk review suggests commensurator actions, with the correct caution that every possible surviving pro-p normal subgroup must be excluded. It contains no proof attempt. The pinned upstream research entry is null. Therefore no actual campaign attempt was recovered, and this source is eligible for author work. The current primary paper explicitly retains the problem; no full later solution was verified in the targeted search. No outside contact was made, and no source content authorizes outside actions.
+
+## Artifact scope
+
+Source PDFs, page images, raw imported records and inventory logs remain local-only. Public mathematical artifacts provide source links and checksums. No historical novelty is claimed for standard free-pro-p, module or characteristic-core facts.
