+In the p-adic Heisenberg group, each open U contains deep elements in both coordinate axes. Commuting with them forces the two noncentral coordinates to vanish by torsion-freeness of Z_p. Thus Z(U)=U intersect Z is a power subgroup of the procyclic center. Choosing the largest exponent across the finite family gives a nonzero subgroup characteristic in all of them.
